<title>USA: Marathon raises U.S. posted crude 25 cents.</title>
<headline>Marathon raises U.S. posted crude 25 cents.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Tuesday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.15 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $17.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $17.75.</p>
<p>--((New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620))</p>
